en after discussion we have arguments for A (agent_3), B (agent_1), D (agent_3 earlier). We need to consider all. Let's evaluate again.\n\nCandidate A: quick correct decisions, excellent attention, calm in crisis, puts concern for others above everything, creates positive atmosphere, difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. Strengths: decision quality, attention, stress resilience, crew cooperation (positive atmosphere). Concerns: communication, egocentric, lack of development.\n\nCandidate B: very conscientious, handles stress very well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills, weak memory for numbers, makes nasty remarks/uncooperative, grumpy. Strengths: reliability, stress resilience, technical competence (weather, computer). Concerns: crew cooperation, memory for numbers (attention/accuracy).\n\nCandidate C: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership, show-off, not open to new ideas, not good at taking criticism, unorganized. Strengths: safety anticipation, complex systems understanding, leadership. Concerns: adaptability, crew cooperation, organization.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, hot temper, moody, loner, know-it-all. Strengths: stress resilience (responds to unexpected events), attention, problem solving, responsibility. Concerns: crew cooperation, temperament.\n\nWe need to decide which candidate best fits overall. The panel hasn't converged. As agent_2, we can either maintain our previous vote for C or shift. Let's weigh.\n\nKey criteria for long-distance pilot: reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, decision quality, attention/accuracy, crew cooperation, professional communication, responsibility, adaptability.\n\nCandidate A: strong decision quality, attention, stress resilience, crew cooperation (positive atmosphere). Weakness: communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education (adaptability). Professional communication: difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric may affect. But crew cooperation seems good.\n\nCandidate B: strong reliability (conscientious), stress resilience, technical competence (weather, computer). Weakness: uncooperative, nasty remarks (crew cooperation, professional communication), weak memory for numbers (attention/accuracy). Adaptability unknown.\n\nCandidate C: strong anticipation, complex connections, spatial vision, leadership (responsibility). Weakness: not open to new ideas (adaptability), not good at taking criticism (crew cooperation), show-off (crew cooperation), unorganized (attention/decision quality). No explicit stress resilience.\n\nCandidate D: stress resilience (responds to unexpected events), attention (concentrate), problem solving (technical competence), responsibility. Weakness: hot temper, moody, loner, know-it-all (crew cooperation, professional communication). Adaptability unknown.\n\nComparing: A seems balanced with strong decision, attention, stress, crew cooperation (positive atmosphere) but communication issues. B has strong stress and technical but crew issues. C has safety anticipation but poor adaptability and crew. D has strong problem solving and responsibility but temperament issues.\n\nWhich is best? The panel may consider that A's communication difficulty could be mitigated with training, while B's uncooperative behavior may be more severe. C's adaptability issues are serious for long-term development. D's temperament may affect crew environment.\n\nThus A might be the best overall. However, we need to consider that A's egocentric and not willing to further education could be problematic for long-term growth. But B's uncooperative behavior could also be dangerous.\n\nGiven the evidence, I think A remains the best overall. As agent_2, we could shift to A, aligning with agent_3. Or we could maintain C if we think safety anticipation is top priority. The panel hasn't converged; we can try to move toward consensus. Since agent_3 strongly supports A, and agent_1 supports B, we could try to find common ground. Perhaps we can propose A as the leading candidate, but we need to justify.\n\nThus I will change my vote to Candidate A, providing reasoning: A's quick correct decisions, excellent attention, calm in crisis, positive crew atmosphere outweigh communication difficulty, and we can address those with training. Also note that B's uncooperative behavior is more severe.\n\nThus produce public message: \"I now support Candidate A because ...\". Provide explicit facts: quick correct decisions, excellent attention, keeps calm in crisis, puts concern for others above everything, creates positive atmosphere. Also mention concerns: difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education, but argue they are less severe.\n\nNow produce METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate A\". Ensure format: {\"agent\":\"agent_2\",\"vote\":\"Candidate A\"}.\n\nProceed."}
